varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{-2x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157456 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ac34a18-053d-5eab-8c2c-bd0f15658186" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Linear ODEs Using Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c0ef841-3242-5caa-a95a-63ce8b7efbf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397008} {:answer/id #uuid "5c1855a8-8668-5bad-a68f-159a347c16e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397009} {:answer/id #uuid "271ee91c-0505-593b-8b96-dcd47eee066b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397010} {:answer/id #uuid "ee36278b-f3db-5dd0-9d77-a7d3896daa39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397011} {:answer/id #uuid "416045ef-0621-54d9-bdb3-7210f39e7ecd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "271ee91c-0505-593b-8b96-dcd47eee066b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397010} :answer-field/id #uuid "23f571bd-1890-5d0b-ad01-ebacf978ce3f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397007} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6613fce0-00ea-54cc-b224-364324bfd38d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397014} {:answer/id #uuid "07ee30c0-36ff-5a79-9a4a-9d08de9626c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397015} {:answer/id #uuid "b953b3c5-d30e-55c3-84a5-1e9cfe455f31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397016} {:answer/id #uuid "a03f2f99-8a72-58f0-91c9-bed5f65cea3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397017} {:answer/id #uuid "40d5b092-c1ca-5934-8385-b0856ab2a919" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397018}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07ee30c0-36ff-5a79-9a4a-9d08de9626c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397015} :answer-field/id #uuid "e359f8f0-477c-59ef-8110-485977df974d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397013} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a8ade83-a027-534c-bd4f-84aa0200d2d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397020} {:answer/id #uuid "a5669714-9638-5173-9084-eb17dd7bd986" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397021} {:answer/id #uuid "ece141df-36de-5040-bd7f-fb517ce895fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397022} {:answer/id #uuid "9075b9b5-02ae-5817-9f6e-b66c5225cfc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397023} {:answer/id #uuid "25c082de-d2be-5ef1-b6ea-07729e875ea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397024}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a8ade83-a027-534c-bd4f-84aa0200d2d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397020} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bedb308-447b-574c-bd8b-26248f559b30" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397019}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a01f9794-773d-5e12-a888-6dc684788a68" :question/math-academy-id "q-337376" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y=5.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}-3{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{3x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{3x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{3x})}^{′}-3(u{e}^{3x}) & =5 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{3x}+3u{e}^{3x}-3u{e}^{3x} & =5 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{3x}+\\cancel{3u{e}^{3x}}-\\cancel{3u{e}^{3x}} & =5 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{3x} & =5 \\\\ {u}^{′} & =5{e}^{-3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =5{e}^{-3x} \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 5{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =-\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{-3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{3x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{3x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{-3x}\\cdot {e}^{3x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478397 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157456 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ac34a18-053d-5eab-8c2c-bd0f15658186" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Linear ODEs Using Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "497197b8-8e76-53b8-86a4-754349398785" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{9x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477880} {:answer/id #uuid "6b46c7a3-36fa-593b-b8a4-fd59ab9a5bab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477957} {:answer/id #uuid "9d326a77-95d4-5330-b18b-381ab039df29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478038} {:answer/id #uuid "ea6289c4-f3fa-56b7-a00e-e7a24c495194" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478197} {:answer/id #uuid "f83737fd-3f7f-562a-8be3-3d48018765df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea6289c4-f3fa-56b7-a00e-e7a24c495194" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478197} :answer-field/id #uuid "1201467f-65cf-51f2-8aac-3e057e5d3832" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478255} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52baabc1-e1ba-5e29-b8f3-ad0c45dac74e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477906} {:answer/id #uuid "d89e3a74-9c5b-597b-9b9b-3427f003e674" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {e}^{4x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478161} {:answer/id #uuid "f4b599cf-98db-5479-bdc6-3133995fc9d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478220} {:answer/id #uuid "faedf7a9-097c-5707-9280-8cb5943bd47d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {e}^{4x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478235}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52baabc1-e1ba-5e29-b8f3-ad0c45dac74e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477906} :answer-field/id #uuid "e241bdb3-4953-5694-b86b-4d66b675e5c3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478351} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4173adb1-df54-5fc4-9563-c32c4b9e631b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-4x}\\int {e}^{4x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477859} {:answer/id #uuid "67a6e201-0a26-525b-9c88-961b30be3674" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-4x}\\int {e}^{4x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477943} {:answer/id #uuid "c30c215f-fb2c-5c3a-8080-c94e9fb9e882" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4x}\\int {e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478120} {:answer/id #uuid "de154aeb-8a61-5641-876a-bb6a4cfbd56d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4x}\\int {e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c30c215f-fb2c-5c3a-8080-c94e9fb9e882" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4x}\\int {e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478120} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffa10310-b897-5f9d-8f7f-96575809586b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478368}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "46fed2b7-c806-57ef-a1e1-bd253db964cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-337443" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4y=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}-4{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{4x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{4x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{4x})}^{′}-4(u{e}^{4x}) & =\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{4x}+4u{e}^{4x}-4u{e}^{4x} & =\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{4x}+\\cancel{4u{e}^{4x}}-\\cancel{4u{e}^{4x}} & =\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{4x} & =\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′} & ={e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & ={e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =\\int {e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{4x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{4x} \\\\  & =\\int {e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {e}^{4x} \\\\  & ={e}^{4x}\\int {e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397080 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157457 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5fb547a-2518-5db9-b1b1-aab8d80328af" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Linear ODEs Using VOP When the Forcing Term is Part of the Complementary Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06d45bf0-b0d2-526d-9ee8-966bee2bf82f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x{e}^{5x}-{e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397082} {:answer/id #uuid "f899948d-7d57-564f-9c17-dc1a4e8c1e4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5x}-x{e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397083} {:answer/id #uuid "cd83b01b-26af-5c69-90f0-dea06d731251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5x}-\\frac{1}{2}x{e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397084} {:answer/id #uuid "ba369324-b632-52dd-b087-db8abad2c3bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x{e}^{5x}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397085}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba369324-b632-52dd-b087-db8abad2c3bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x{e}^{5x}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397085} :answer-field/id #uuid "02bdb63b-0f09-5614-88a9-63938cc89b6d" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397081} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5bc26fc-760a-5855-9195-3473708b71ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-{e}^{-10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397087} {:answer/id #uuid "80570deb-15eb-5c3a-beac-50b739cab35b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{2}x{e}^{-10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397088} {:answer/id #uuid "32a1c91a-9d5b-5cd5-ac23-19ae0f28b96e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397089} {:answer/id #uuid "f12ce1c7-e215-555b-8e8d-d49be3f26f0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-x{e}^{-10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32a1c91a-9d5b-5cd5-ac23-19ae0f28b96e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397089} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddc85c1c-2146-58a2-8708-42bac8c22805" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397086} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4cbf3f92-2ab9-584c-9c0e-47d30d63d2a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397092} {:answer/id #uuid "d41e52db-7e65-579d-9821-9e969bdbaf23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397093} {:answer/id #uuid "104a2da1-9f11-510a-9e86-88dce1ddf0c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397094} {:answer/id #uuid "ffc049b9-0f4d-5a90-aa1e-01e88bb54d2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{15x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397095} {:answer/id #uuid "fe3e4f63-8e52-5102-b305-3e0c04fc80b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "104a2da1-9f11-510a-9e86-88dce1ddf0c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397094} :answer-field/id #uuid "23391fc0-0d97-510f-b68a-65d0d3b75416" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397091}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5bf23900-2f3d-53c0-9448-69b2b01a2a2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-337488" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5y=10\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}-5{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{5x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{5x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{5x})}^{′}-5(u{e}^{5x}) & =10\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{5x}+5u{e}^{5x}-5u{e}^{5x} & =10\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{5x}+\\cancel{5u{e}^{5x}}-\\cancel{5u{e}^{5x}} & =10\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{5x} & =10\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′} & =10{e}^{-5x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x=\\frac{{e}^{5x}+{e}^{-5x}}{2}\n$$\n\nour equation for $u$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =10{e}^{-5x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\  & =10{e}^{-5x}(\\frac{{e}^{5x}+{e}^{-5x}}{2}) \\\\  & =5{e}^{-5x}({e}^{5x}+{e}^{-5x}) \\\\  & =5+5{e}^{-10x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =5+5{e}^{-10x} \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 5+5{e}^{-10x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =5x-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-10x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{5x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{5x} \\\\  & =5x{e}^{5x}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-5x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478442 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157457 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5fb547a-2518-5db9-b1b1-aab8d80328af" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Linear ODEs Using VOP When the Forcing Term is Part of the Complementary Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20068763-68a2-57b5-9b52-fcdbf1673fb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477796} {:answer/id #uuid "44976bea-1d15-5380-8acc-cf59a6c4390f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{e}^{6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 175921864